  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1150 AM CDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nCooler overnights and mornings will persist through early next\nweek thanks to drier air in place. Higher terrain across the\nPlateau are forecast to have lows in the upper 50s Monday and\nTuesday mornings.\n\nTroughing will make a slow progression to the east mid to late\nnext week. This should open the door for an increase in moisture\nfrom the west. Continued mid- to upper-level flow will persist\nfrom the northwest providing a corridor for shortwaves to move\nthrough the area. These passing disturbances support the low to \nmedium rain and storm chances most days next week. Temperatures \nare generally near seasonal norms.",
